      "writtenOn": "2026-01-21T18:51:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e More precisely the need to call UseBufferInternal judiciously in backends.\n\nIt might be easier to add a bool to BufferBase that disables the assertion in MarkUsedInPendingCommands(). That bool would be false for externally allocated buffers and true for internal temp/staging buffers. That way there is no need add UseBufferInternal() for all the temp/staging buffers?\n\n\u003e So yeah I think that\u0027s an alternative, but I think the current approach could be landed if doing this change seemed too onerous.\n\nI think the main complexities of using a mutex to guard mLastUsageSerial.\n\n1. Building a list of buffers to update mLastUsageSerial while mutex is locked would require an extra iteration through commands when validation is disabled. That would add some cost.\n1. Removing all the existing calls to MarkUsedInPendingCommands() that happen while backend submit implementation issues work to backend API is non-trivial to do.",
      "parentUuid": "e92b9935_936cc7b7",
      "revId": "ab046652b43a65dbd9b4bae559fa4d91e69940ea",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
